# Supabase Data Access Patterns

- Keep Supabase client creation centralized and typed; avoid duplicating setup logic.
- Keep DB/API access in services and route handlers, not in presentation components.
- Validate external inputs at boundaries (params, forms, payloads) before DB/API operations.
- Handle loading, empty, and error states explicitly in user-facing screens.
- Keep writes explicit and map failures to clear domain errors.
- If `@tanstack/react-query` is introduced, use stable query keys and explicit cache invalidation.
- If React Query is not used, keep data-fetching logic simple and predictable.
